From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: x <x@x>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 13:33:43 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Serein: render emoji-presentation clusters from a color font
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Fallback picked a face per base char and ignored emoji presentation, so a text font earlier in the chain with a plain glyph (a math font's ♾, a symbol font's 🆕) beat the color emoji font, and the system provider asked text fonts before the emoji family. Clusters with emoji presentation (default, or U+FE0F) now prefer a face with a color glyph, asking the providers for one, and the system provider queries the emoji family first. Text presentation is unchanged. Adds two tiny fixture fonts and a regression test.
